  "id": "763d69c2-6d0f-4c9c-b06d-cbdcf5182dcf",
  "title": "Amelia Earhart's Plane Debris Identified as Clumps of Trees",
  "summary": "Researchers confirmed that an object first spotted on satellite imagery in 2020 was a clump of trees, which has led to speculation about Amelia Earhart's disappearance. However, the expedition to the remote Pacific Island atoll has left the search for the pilot unresolved.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Researchers found a clump of trees in the remote Pacific Island atoll off Nikumaroro, which they believe could have been Amelia Earhart's plane.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A US expedition to the atoll was drawn to investigate the metallic glint in the waters, but no evidence was found of a plane or a smoking gun.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The expedition led by Purdue University concluded that the mystery remains unsolved after no conclusive findings were obtained",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
