    {
      "title": "Amelia Earhart researchers leave remote atoll empty-handed after ‘plane debris’ found to be a clump of trees",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/amelia-earhart-purdue-expedition-clump-of-trees-nikumaroro-kiribati",
      "description": "<p>Expedition was drawn to Nikumaroro after spotting what was described as a metallic glint in waters off uninhabited island</p><p>A US expedition that voyaged to a remote Pacific island in the hope of solving the mystery of what happened to pioneering pilot Amelia Earhart has said an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/12/amelia-earhart-lost-plane-remote-pacific-atoll-expedition\">object they suspected to be her plane</a> was a clump of washed-up trees.</p><p>“Unfortunately, we weren’t able to find that smoking gun,” said Steve Schultz of Purdue University, standing on the sand in front of a blue lagoon on the atoll of Nikumaroro, about halfway between Australia and Hawaii.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/amelia-earhart-purdue-expedition-clump-of-trees-nikumaroro-kiribati\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
